{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1482554-i-would-absolutely-love-a-dark-eras-style-approach-for-a-2e-mirrors-book","id":1482554,"title":"I would absolutely love a Dark Eras-style approach for a 2e Mirrors book.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-31T17:04:48-07:00","id":1482554,"title":"I would absolutely love a Dark Eras-style approach for a 2e Mirrors book.","content":"Go ahead and bring updates to the five settings already given in Mirrors (Revealed, Destroyed, Dark Fantasy, Bleeding Edge, Infinite Macabre), maybe fold Innocents in there as well.<br /> <br /> The trick is that I'm not clever enough to come up with new shards that could be incorporated; most of my ideas are too similar to the ones listed above, and would feel redundant. Maybe expanding a few of them into more specific and fleshed-out examples of what they consist of -- Revealed could be broken down into different ways that the supernatural is exposed as real and the ramifications for each scenario (a global hunt, monsters become celebrities, new cities form entirely around a specific type of supernatural, and so on) and Destroyed could split off into different apocalypse scenarios (humans are hunted/farmed, all mortals are extinct and only supernaturals are left, zombie/natural/alien apocalypse).<br /> <br /> Maybe, if possible, it could be fun to do crossovers with other Onyx Path properties like Scion as part of a 2e Mirrors book. I'm not entirely sure how (or if) the licensing would work out here, however.<br /> <br /> What ideas would you have for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26615-runomai","name":"RuNoMai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T18:49:42-07:00","id":1482699,"title":"","content":"Given there's definite interest to go and revisit at least one of the shards (Infinite Macabre),this might not be a bad way to go about it. Hell, you could break it up by section so you have the universal rules and tools on how to make your own, and then have a variety of specific kinds of setting in that section. Wouldn't mind doing Into the Void(Space Age of Exploration meets the Divine Comedy) and The Reflection Galaxy Cluster in that way for the Infinite Macabre, at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-01-2022, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}